WEBVTT

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:07.050
Well. Look who came back.

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:11.390
Welcome back to Steadfast Men. This is Lesson Two.

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:14.530
It's called You Are Not Crazy.

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:16.270
Here's how this goes.

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:20.530
First, the noise, and what Paul says about the wind.

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:23.650
Second, where that fight came from.

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:26.990
Third, what the fight does to a man.

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:31.170
He waits, he performs, and he carries shame.

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:34.310
Fourth, what God said first.

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:38.770
Fifth, how to own your part without carrying the world's.

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:43.290
And last, one sentence you can stand on, and one move.

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:48.870
Last lesson you and I sat with a quiet Tuesday, and you got the first mark.

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:54.610
Stop Waiting. And you got the small yes, the one that's still standing after the

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:55.690
feeling goes home.

00:00:56.220 --> 00:01:01.830
I also gave you one move. A meal with the phone in another room, and a text to one

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:02.190
man.

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:03.750
So how'd it go?

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:07.270
Maybe halfway. Halfway counts too.

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:11.050
If this is your first one, you didn't miss the only door in.

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:13.890
Pull up a chair. Nobody's a guest here.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:16.790
You and I take this one lesson at a time.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:24.010
Here's what I'd bet happened. You hit an ordinary day, and you meant to say the

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:25.050
small yes.

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:28.530
And a voice in your head said, do it this way.

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:33.410
Then another one said, no, a real man does the opposite.

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:35.030
So you stood there.

00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:39.090
Tuesday in one hand. Two sets of orders in the other.

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:42.110
That's what this lesson is after.

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:43.430
Not the day.

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:45.670
The noise on the day.

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:47.090
Hear it plain.

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:49.570
You are not crazy.

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:56.050
You want a straight answer about what a man is for, and you can't get two people to

00:01:55.980 --> 00:01:56.570
agree.

00:01:57.040 --> 00:01:58.390
That's a good want.

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:02.030
The mess you feel isn't coming from a broken head.

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:05.590
It's coming from somewhere. Let's go find where.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:09.030
I'll tell on myself first.

00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:15.610
Years ago, a man I worked around told me, if you're serious, the work gets the first

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:18.070
of you. Your family gets what's left.

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:20.550
If you're decent, that's enough.

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:23.650
I nodded. I heard grit in it.

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:28.350
Around then, an older man in a group I sat in said the opposite.

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:34.110
He said, if your people get the leftovers, you already answered the question.

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:36.090
You just answered it small.

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:39.290
So I tried to obey both.

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:40.530
Same night.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:43.990
I stayed late so the first man could be proud.

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:47.570
Then I came home loud and helpful for the second one.

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:51.030
I unloaded the dishwasher like I was on the clock.

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:53.770
My wife watched from the doorway.

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:56.670
She didn't argue. She didn't have to.

00:02:57.460 --> 00:03:01.370
I'd turned helping into a show, and she could hear the show.

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:06.530
Nothing says I'm right here with you like slamming the silverware drawer.

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:09.390
I wanted them both proud of me.

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:13.830
Neither one lived in my house. She didn't need a contest.

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:17.210
She needed a man who was actually in the room.

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:20.630
I went to bed sure I'd failed them both.

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:22.370
I probably had.

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:26.530
One voice calls you selfish if you stay with the work.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:29.350
Another calls you soft if you leave it.

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:34.210
You can hear both before supper and still not know which door is yours.

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:36.410
And both of them meant well.

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:42.290
Both were half right. But a man can't live by two half-rights that won't sit at the

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:43.130
same table.

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:49.410
So you pick one on Monday, the other on Thursday, and feel guilty both days.

00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:53.990
Ephesians chapter four, verse fourteen.

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:59.850
"Then we will no longer be infants, tossed back and forth by the waves, and blown

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:04.950
here and there by every wind of teaching and by the cunning and craftiness of people

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:06.430
in their deceitful scheming."

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:11.350
Tossed back and forth. Blown here and there.

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:14.110
Paul doesn't pretend the wind isn't blowing.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:17.130
He names it. Some of it honest and wrong.

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:21.230
Some of it not so honest. And notice who gets tossed.

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:26.110
Not a wicked man. An infant. A man nobody finished raising.

00:04:27.140 --> 00:04:30.290
A boat getting thrown around doesn't mean the boat is crazy.

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:31.730
It means there's weather.

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:37.030
Last lesson, a boy put his childish ways behind him on purpose.

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:39.850
Here Paul comes at it from the other side.

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:44.650
Growing up means standing in the wind without deciding the wind is your fault.

00:04:46.520 --> 00:04:48.990
You didn't invent the fight in your head.

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:50.530
Neither did I.

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:52.970
You and I inherited it.

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:56.370
There was a time a boy could see the work.

00:04:56.840 --> 00:05:01.290
He stood next to a man, and the knowing was in the man's hands.

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:03.930
Now the work is across town.

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:07.610
Or down the hall on a laptop, door shut.

00:05:08.180 --> 00:05:11.470
The boy sees his dad leave and come home tired.

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:14.370
Everything in the middle is a rumor.

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:19.550
So nobody hands him one sentence for both places a man has to live.

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:21.330
He grabs pieces.

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:24.030
An uncle at a cookout hands him one.

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:26.170
A group text hands him the other.

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:27.850
He nods at both.

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:31.730
Then he grows up and tries to obey the whole pile.

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:35.490
When it won't add up, he figures the problem is him.

00:05:36.760 --> 00:05:38.890
Then a lot of rooms got shy.

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:43.190
Saying God made a man on purpose started to feel risky.

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:46.210
The old words got treated like a problem.

00:05:46.580 --> 00:05:50.670
Provide. Protect. Decide. Stay.

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:53.930
A man could feel accused just for carrying them.

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:57.930
Then the same world mocked the man who wouldn't grow up.

00:05:58.260 --> 00:06:00.570
Wouldn't stay. Wouldn't decide.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:04.550
It gave both orders. It just never said so out loud.

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:08.910
One clip on your phone says strong makes you a threat.

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:12.470
The next says if you aren't strong, you're finished.

00:06:12.880 --> 00:06:16.930
Same pocket. A coach tells a young man, take the room.

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:21.330
Be loud. His first boss tells him, don't make a ripple.

00:06:21.620 --> 00:06:24.490
The ones who last around here are the quiet ones.

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:27.850
He's twenty-two and already has a headache.

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:30.570
And nobody admits they handed him both.

00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:33.310
I'm not swinging at the church.

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:34.330
I'm in it.

00:06:34.820 --> 00:06:40.210
But it got nervous about a plain sentence, so it handed out soft words or loud ones.

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:43.890
Neither told a man what to do when he came home used up.

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:46.870
He got a pile. He needed a path.

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:53.250
Try this. Name two instructions about being a man that can't both be true.

00:06:54.660 --> 00:06:56.250
Yeah. That came quick.

00:06:56.800 --> 00:07:01.390
If you can name two orders that fight, you're not confused because you're slow.

00:07:01.780 --> 00:07:04.110
You're confused because you were listening.

00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:08.750
That's a man paying attention to voices that should have agreed and didn't.

00:07:10.640 --> 00:07:13.230
Genesis chapter three, verse ten.

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:14.830
"He answered,

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:19.490
I heard you in the garden, and I was afraid because I was naked;

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:20.810
so I hid."

00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:26.070
That's the first man, right after the first wrong turn.

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:30.450
God comes walking in the cool of the day, calling for him.

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:34.910
And the answer is afraid, and covered, and hid.

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:38.770
That's still what a man does when the orders won't agree.

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:41.910
The fight does three things to a man.

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:43.470
I've done all three.

00:07:43.960 --> 00:07:45.170
I'd bet you have too.

00:07:46.220 --> 00:07:48.750
First, he hides by waiting.

00:07:49.420 --> 00:07:54.590
If every direction has been scolded by somebody, standing still starts to look

00:07:54.520 --> 00:07:55.190
polite.

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:57.050
You call it patience.

00:07:57.800 --> 00:08:00.670
I stood at my own kitchen sink once and hid.

00:08:01.420 --> 00:08:05.650
I had a true sentence ready for my wife, about a bill we'd been dodging.

00:08:06.020 --> 00:08:09.670
Not a crisis. A decision with both our names on it.

00:08:10.100 --> 00:08:12.630
The plate in my hand was already dry.

00:08:13.080 --> 00:08:15.570
I kept drying it. Five minutes.

00:08:15.920 --> 00:08:16.770
Maybe ten.

00:08:17.460 --> 00:08:19.470
Then I asked if we were out of dish soap.

00:08:20.140 --> 00:08:22.930
Soap had an answer. The sentence didn't.

00:08:23.360 --> 00:08:25.170
The bill didn't leave the house.

00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:28.090
It sat down at the table and got heavier.

00:08:28.540 --> 00:08:30.030
And she quit bringing it up.

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:35.630
Not because it got settled. Because soap was the only answer she ever got.

00:08:36.680 --> 00:08:38.190
I called it being careful.

00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:41.610
Careful can be a stall with a clean shirt on.

00:08:42.240 --> 00:08:46.330
Have you gone quiet because quiet felt safer than picking a side?

00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:48.270
Me too.

00:08:49.580 --> 00:08:52.470
Second, he covers by performing.

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:57.410
The first thing that man did in the garden was sew something to hide behind.

00:08:57.880 --> 00:09:02.830
If nobody handed you one steady way, you start fitting whatever room you're in.

00:09:03.460 --> 00:09:04.750
I got good at the fit.

00:09:05.260 --> 00:09:07.550
An easy laugh when the talk was loose.

00:09:07.960 --> 00:09:10.150
A serious nod when it got heavy.

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:12.530
I wasn't trying to fool anybody.

00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:14.430
I was matching the temperature.

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:18.710
I've answered the same question two ways in one hour.

00:09:19.220 --> 00:09:22.070
On the back steps with a buddy, the easy version.

00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:23.650
Then in the kitchen.

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:26.690
Same facts. Different man talking.

00:09:27.140 --> 00:09:28.730
Nobody asked me to switch.

00:09:29.220 --> 00:09:29.910
I offered.

00:09:30.760 --> 00:09:33.770
I've been a whole committee before the porch light came on.

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:35.650
None of them was quite me.

00:09:36.240 --> 00:09:36.850
They were,

00:09:37.340 --> 00:09:38.190
what's the word.

00:09:38.860 --> 00:09:39.470
Rented.

00:09:40.020 --> 00:09:42.850
And a rented man goes back when the day's done.

00:09:43.900 --> 00:09:45.110
Here's the tender part.

00:09:45.740 --> 00:09:47.390
That man isn't a villain.

00:09:47.860 --> 00:09:52.090
Nobody gave him one way and stayed with it, so he copies the room.

00:09:52.640 --> 00:09:54.270
Copying wears you out.

00:09:54.820 --> 00:09:57.490
From the outside, people call it competence.

00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:02.150
You can stop auditioning. The room can survive the real man.

00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:05.530
A performance gets you through a lot of rooms.

00:10:05.940 --> 00:10:07.570
Not through your own front door.

00:10:08.060 --> 00:10:10.910
The people who live with you know which one is you.

00:10:12.780 --> 00:10:13.370
Third,

00:10:13.900 --> 00:10:15.250
and I'll go slower here.

00:10:16.040 --> 00:10:17.590
He carries shame.

00:10:18.660 --> 00:10:23.570
Hand a man orders that argue with each other, and he doesn't blame the orders.

00:10:24.040 --> 00:10:25.990
He puts himself on trial.

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:30.570
And he won't say it out loud, because that feels like making it official.

00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:36.330
So he carries it down the hardware aisle, through the school pickup line, into the

00:10:36.300 --> 00:10:37.890
dark of his own room.

00:10:38.580 --> 00:10:40.990
He calls that being realistic.

00:10:41.600 --> 00:10:46.070
It's a good man prosecuting himself for a contradiction he didn't write.

00:10:47.120 --> 00:10:48.430
I've carried one of those.

00:10:49.140 --> 00:10:52.270
I thought if I said it, it'd be the last word on me.

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:55.030
So I smiled and kept moving.

00:10:56.900 --> 00:10:58.870
I knew a man I'll call Ray.

00:10:59.380 --> 00:11:00.230
Not his name.

00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:02.830
I knew his truck better than I knew him.

00:11:03.620 --> 00:11:08.630
One afternoon he and I ended up at a parts counter, both waiting on a belt for a

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:09.230
dryer.

00:11:09.840 --> 00:11:11.270
The clerk went in the back.

00:11:11.920 --> 00:11:14.310
Ray's hands were nicked up from the day.

00:11:14.760 --> 00:11:16.510
He kept his eyes on the counter.

00:11:17.200 --> 00:11:21.030
Ray looked wrung out, and it had nothing to do with laundry.

00:11:22.220 --> 00:11:26.630
Out of nowhere he told me he'd been saving up rules since he was a kid.

00:11:27.080 --> 00:11:30.750
His old man said, a man doesn't explain himself.

00:11:31.140 --> 00:11:33.430
You do the thing and keep moving.

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:38.570
His first boss said, if you can't explain it, you don't understand it.

00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:39.850
So speak up.

00:11:40.360 --> 00:11:43.330
Two rules, both sure of themselves.

00:11:43.720 --> 00:11:45.590
They'd never have shared a table.

00:11:46.240 --> 00:11:47.710
Then he got married.

00:11:48.180 --> 00:11:50.870
His wife asked him not to go quiet on her.

00:11:51.300 --> 00:11:54.250
His brother told him, don't you give up the wheel.

00:11:54.680 --> 00:11:57.270
A man who gives it up is already done.

00:11:57.780 --> 00:12:01.670
I'm not siding with the brother, and I'm not making her the problem.

00:12:02.100 --> 00:12:05.290
Both of them loved him. The orders fought.

00:12:06.560 --> 00:12:09.370
Ray slid a scrap of paper out of his wallet.

00:12:09.920 --> 00:12:12.090
Two lines in his own printing.

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:15.790
The crease had gone white from years of folding.

00:12:16.300 --> 00:12:19.550
He read it in his truck before he walked into his own house.

00:12:20.300 --> 00:12:22.330
One line said, speak.

00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:25.610
The other said, don't you make a fuss.

00:12:26.320 --> 00:12:26.890
He said,

00:12:27.480 --> 00:12:30.670
"Wes, if I was smarter, these would fit."

00:12:32.040 --> 00:12:34.970
I had a little speech ready, with a bow on top.

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:38.590
I heard myself start, and I shut it down.

00:12:39.160 --> 00:12:41.830
He needed the truth in a smaller size.

00:12:42.300 --> 00:12:43.030
So I said,

00:12:43.540 --> 00:12:48.330
"Ray, you're not slow. Those two lines were never gonna shake hands.

00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:53.170
You've been carrying a fight in your wallet and calling it a personal failure."

00:12:54.520 --> 00:12:57.250
He didn't rebuild his life at a parts counter.

00:12:57.700 --> 00:13:00.250
The clerk came back with the wrong belt, actually.

00:13:00.800 --> 00:13:04.450
But Ray folded that scrap once instead of twice.

00:13:04.880 --> 00:13:07.010
Like it was smaller than it had been.

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:09.910
Sometimes that's where it starts.

00:13:10.500 --> 00:13:15.750
You see the fight was handed to you, and you quit treating your own name as the

00:13:15.680 --> 00:13:16.430
charge.

00:13:18.260 --> 00:13:22.350
I don't want any of this resting on my opinion, or on Ray's wallet.

00:13:22.820 --> 00:13:26.930
So go back two chapters, before anybody was afraid of anything.

00:13:27.360 --> 00:13:29.910
Genesis chapter one, verse twenty-seven.

00:13:30.480 --> 00:13:36.790
"So God created mankind in his own image, in the image of God he created them; male

00:13:36.740 --> 00:13:38.590
and female he created them."

00:13:40.060 --> 00:13:40.890
Created.

00:13:41.380 --> 00:13:44.410
Not assembled by committee. Not left to chance.

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:48.110
Male and female is on purpose in that sentence.

00:13:48.500 --> 00:13:51.010
And the man had nothing to show for himself yet.

00:13:51.340 --> 00:13:52.050
No résumé.

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:55.070
God called the making good anyway.

00:13:55.420 --> 00:13:57.270
He wasn't embarrassed of what he made.

00:13:57.600 --> 00:14:00.210
People got embarrassed later, me included.

00:14:00.540 --> 00:14:03.570
Quietly, one careful sermon at a time.

00:14:04.640 --> 00:14:08.970
So that sense you've got, that being a man is a real thing, is right.

00:14:09.300 --> 00:14:12.930
It's not a costume. It's not a flaw in how he built you.

00:14:13.320 --> 00:14:17.470
It's one way the image of God walks around in an actual life.

00:14:17.860 --> 00:14:20.410
It was his idea. He wasn't guessing.

00:14:21.480 --> 00:14:23.210
And your other sense is right too.

00:14:23.600 --> 00:14:25.750
The orders you were handed don't agree.

00:14:26.180 --> 00:14:29.410
If you got turned around, look hard at what you were handed.

00:14:29.720 --> 00:14:32.110
Your own mind isn't the first suspect.

00:14:32.440 --> 00:14:38.810
The Book hasn't been silent. People got busy, or clever, and called a pile a path.

00:14:39.220 --> 00:14:43.370
So wanting a plain word about what a man is for is a good hunger.

00:14:43.700 --> 00:14:47.990
Don't apologize for it. That hunger is part of how he made you.

00:14:49.840 --> 00:14:51.550
Here's the part you'll want to skip.

00:14:52.100 --> 00:14:55.970
Part of the gap is yours. Part of it was handed to you.

00:14:56.380 --> 00:14:57.670
You own both.

00:14:58.220 --> 00:15:02.810
If you only own the world's part, the confusion becomes a hiding place.

00:15:03.280 --> 00:15:04.670
I've rented that place.

00:15:05.140 --> 00:15:08.490
If the orders fight, nobody can say I missed mine.

00:15:09.040 --> 00:15:12.770
I called that humble. It was a way to stay untested.

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:17.510
Or maybe you went the other way and pleaded guilty to the whole mess.

00:15:18.020 --> 00:15:22.810
You called yourself broken, when mostly you were worn out by a contradiction.

00:15:23.380 --> 00:15:26.390
That's swinging at yourself with somebody else's stick.

00:15:26.920 --> 00:15:28.830
Where you checked out, say so.

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:32.110
Where the orders fought, name the orders.

00:15:32.480 --> 00:15:36.230
Keep both on the table, and don't let one swallow the other.

00:15:36.760 --> 00:15:41.470
I've watched a man blame the whole world at lunch and blame himself by supper.

00:15:41.980 --> 00:15:45.710
Neither is honest. Both are easier than the truth.

00:15:46.780 --> 00:15:49.850
I watched a shrug get passed off as wisdom once.

00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:55.750
At a church breakfast, a younger man asked, plain, what's a man supposed to be for?

00:15:56.340 --> 00:16:01.890
An older man I trusted leaned his chair back and said, shoot, nobody really knows.

00:16:02.240 --> 00:16:03.470
Just don't be a jerk.

00:16:03.980 --> 00:16:07.550
The younger man looked relieved, like the test got called off.

00:16:08.140 --> 00:16:09.950
I get why the older man said it.

00:16:10.260 --> 00:16:15.670
He was tired of loud opinions. But that young man walked out poorer than he walked

00:16:15.580 --> 00:16:15.930
in.

00:16:16.520 --> 00:16:18.670
A shrug can pass for peace.

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:22.110
A younger man will copy it, and it won't hold him up.

00:16:22.560 --> 00:16:23.750
A sentence will.

00:16:25.600 --> 00:16:28.210
Where you're sitting changes the bruise.

00:16:28.680 --> 00:16:32.050
If you're young, the guessing isn't proof you're behind.

00:16:32.440 --> 00:16:34.730
You got handed a loud pile early.

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:39.130
If you're single, a wife isn't the starting line of manhood.

00:16:39.460 --> 00:16:42.770
You can aim a life before anybody shares your name.

00:16:43.240 --> 00:16:46.410
If you're married, providing is a real weight.

00:16:46.820 --> 00:16:49.470
Honor it. It's just not the whole of you.

00:16:49.960 --> 00:16:53.990
If you've been hurt, you can be wounded and still not be crazy.

00:16:54.520 --> 00:16:59.150
Naming the bad orders clears the table, so you can see which weight is yours.

00:16:59.680 --> 00:17:03.770
If you're older, somebody younger needs you to help him sort the pile.

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:09.090
And if the job's going great, hitting every room's target isn't knowing who to be in

00:17:08.980 --> 00:17:09.930
your own kitchen.

00:17:10.980 --> 00:17:14.610
So what do you do with a pile? You don't need a taller one.

00:17:14.920 --> 00:17:19.310
You need one sentence that holds weight when nobody's handing out credit.

00:17:19.620 --> 00:17:21.470
You got the start of it last lesson.

00:17:21.840 --> 00:17:25.570
Stop Waiting. You'll hear the whole thing before I'm done.

00:17:25.960 --> 00:17:30.890
It's simpler than the pile. And it's harder, because you have to live it on a flat

00:17:30.800 --> 00:17:33.430
afternoon, when the feeling's gone home.

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:36.230
Let me land it.

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:41.270
The confusion is in the world. You were handed orders that fight.

00:17:41.640 --> 00:17:45.930
And you're not crazy for wanting one clear word about what a man is for.

00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:49.810
The wind is real. So is the hiding.

00:17:50.140 --> 00:17:55.750
Afraid, so I hid. You wait, you perform, you carry the shame.

00:17:56.040 --> 00:17:59.610
But before any of that, God made you on purpose.

00:17:59.940 --> 00:18:04.010
Male and female, in his image. Never a costume.

00:18:04.300 --> 00:18:08.670
Never a mood. So own both. Name the orders that fought.

00:18:08.980 --> 00:18:12.670
Own the part that's yours. Don't use the world as a blanket.

00:18:13.060 --> 00:18:15.630
What I hope you carry out of here is relief.

00:18:16.000 --> 00:18:17.850
Not the kind that lets you off the hook.

00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:20.630
The kind that lets you pick up the right thing.

00:18:21.020 --> 00:18:25.130
Your part is still yours. The rest was never yours.

00:18:25.420 --> 00:18:29.110
Somebody handed it to you, and you were too decent to put it down.

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:32.930
Get your workbook open to Lesson Two.

00:18:33.380 --> 00:18:36.470
Don't polish this. Ugly and true will do.

00:18:37.100 --> 00:18:41.110
Three questions. Stop the video after each one and write.

00:18:41.520 --> 00:18:46.810
First. Name two instructions you were handed about being a man that contradict each

00:18:46.740 --> 00:18:48.990
other. Where did each one come from?

00:18:49.420 --> 00:18:53.070
Home. A job. A screen. A church.

00:18:53.380 --> 00:18:53.930
A buddy.

00:18:54.480 --> 00:18:55.610
One sentence each.

00:18:57.980 --> 00:19:00.750
Second. Which one is closer right now?

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:03.570
You wait. You perform for the room.

00:19:03.940 --> 00:19:06.670
Or you carry a quiet hum of shame.

00:19:06.980 --> 00:19:09.770
Write the true one. Not the flattering one.

00:19:12.100 --> 00:19:12.630
Third.

00:19:13.200 --> 00:19:16.870
In one sentence, what do you believe a man is supposed to do?

00:19:17.540 --> 00:19:21.890
Not the one you wish. The one you'd say if nobody was grading you.

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:27.010
Last lesson I asked you to text one man.

00:19:27.460 --> 00:19:30.650
This lesson, I'm asking you to tell him the truth.

00:19:31.080 --> 00:19:33.510
Not the committee. Not the rented man.

00:19:33.960 --> 00:19:34.330
You.

00:19:35.380 --> 00:19:36.950
So here's your one move.

00:19:37.640 --> 00:19:38.050
One.

00:19:38.620 --> 00:19:40.930
Sit down with one man you trust.

00:19:41.320 --> 00:19:44.950
Tell him the orders you were handed, and which one you've been obeying.

00:19:45.300 --> 00:19:48.290
Then read him your sentence, and ask for his.

00:19:48.800 --> 00:19:52.730
Don't explain first. Explaining is how a man hides.

00:19:53.100 --> 00:19:55.790
And don't rescue him from his with advice.

00:19:56.220 --> 00:19:58.410
Advice can be a nice way to leave.

00:19:58.960 --> 00:20:03.970
Write the sentence today. A private project you mean to finish later is how this

00:20:03.900 --> 00:20:04.870
part dies.

00:20:05.940 --> 00:20:07.710
One more line for your handwriting.

00:20:08.120 --> 00:20:13.530
The confusion is in the world. I'm not crazy for wanting one clear word.

00:20:13.940 --> 00:20:14.950
Write it once.

00:20:17.300 --> 00:20:19.590
Now the four marks, like I promised.

00:20:20.080 --> 00:20:26.270
A steadfast man stops waiting, picks up the weight, goes first, and works for God's

00:20:26.200 --> 00:20:27.790
pay, not the room's.

00:20:29.460 --> 00:20:32.130
Set down what God never asked you to carry.

00:20:32.440 --> 00:20:33.790
Pick up what's yours.

00:20:34.260 --> 00:20:38.130
Then say your sentence out loud to a man who'll say his back.

00:20:39.180 --> 00:20:43.230
Next lesson we look at all four marks, and stay longer on one.

00:20:43.600 --> 00:20:46.190
Go find your man, and tell him the truth.
